WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.681 --> 00:00:03.185
- [Scott] I, personally,
always had a bit of an affinity

00:00:03.185 --> 00:00:05.765
towards finding things that're unexpected.

00:00:05.765 --> 00:00:07.397
So, I find it incredible that,

00:00:07.397 --> 00:00:08.275
here in Dubai,

00:00:08.275 --> 00:00:10.853
we do have this world-class
surfing community,

00:00:10.853 --> 00:00:12.458
and we do have waves.

00:00:12.458 --> 00:00:14.585
Dubai's typically known
for the high-rises,

00:00:14.585 --> 00:00:16.613
and five-star luxury.

00:00:16.613 --> 00:00:19.507
I think this kind of bohemian,
underground surf-culture,

00:00:19.507 --> 00:00:20.352
mixing with that,

00:00:20.352 --> 00:00:23.222
is just a pretty beautiful thing.

00:00:23.222 --> 00:00:26.639
(tinkling ambient music)

00:00:29.635 --> 00:00:30.687
My name is Scott Chambers,

00:00:30.687 --> 00:00:33.875
and I'm the founder and
CEO of Surf House Dubai.

00:00:33.875 --> 00:00:36.122
I was born in Sharjah in the UAE.

00:00:36.122 --> 00:00:38.927
The UAE was a very different
place back then, in the ‘90s,

00:00:38.927 --> 00:00:42.609
and yeah, surfing culture
was really non-existent

00:00:42.609 --> 00:00:43.609
at the time.

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:46.024
Over the last 25 years,

00:00:46.024 --> 00:00:48.662
the surf community's grown tremendously.

00:00:48.662 --> 00:00:51.284
Dubai actually sits in the ideal location

00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:52.512
to pick up the best swells

00:00:52.512 --> 00:00:53.874
that come through the Arabian Gulf.

00:00:53.874 --> 00:00:55.772
It just makes it a very favorable place

00:00:55.772 --> 00:00:58.058
to learn how to surf.

00:00:58.058 --> 00:01:00.252
My friendship with Fahim
started 20 years back,

00:01:00.252 --> 00:01:01.704
when we were in high school together.

00:01:01.704 --> 00:01:04.070
We shared a love for
the water and for surfing.

00:01:04.070 --> 00:01:06.687
- Scott and a group of his
friends were the first surfers

00:01:06.687 --> 00:01:08.269
in Dubai,

00:01:08.269 --> 00:01:10.153
a long time ago,

00:01:10.153 --> 00:01:11.404
uh, and I saw them out in the water,

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:13.938
and I wanted to do what they were doing.

00:01:13.938 --> 00:01:16.602
And I remember paddling out for my first time,

00:01:16.602 --> 00:01:18.156
and catching that first wave,

00:01:18.156 --> 00:01:20.239
and I was totally hooked.

00:01:21.204 --> 00:01:23.732
As Scott grew the surfing community,

00:01:23.732 --> 00:01:24.939
there was an opportunity for me

00:01:24.939 --> 00:01:27.074
to come on board as a
partner in the business,

00:01:27.074 --> 00:01:29.845
and us to create this new embassy,

00:01:29.845 --> 00:01:32.012
for the surfing community.

00:01:33.678 --> 00:01:35.793
Dubai in the United
Arab Emirates is a place

00:01:35.793 --> 00:01:38.808
that supports small businesses to grow,

00:01:38.808 --> 00:01:42.975
and for people to really create
really innovative concepts.

00:01:44.319 --> 00:01:46.747
The exhilaration and the
connection with the ocean

00:01:46.747 --> 00:01:49.182
is something that just can't be described.

00:01:49.182 --> 00:01:51.166
It promotes that ocean culture,

00:01:51.166 --> 00:01:53.847
that ocean-minded, uh, consciousness,

00:01:53.847 --> 00:01:55.639
of, of our environment.

00:01:55.639 --> 00:01:59.310
Surfing transcends
cultures, nationalities.

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:01.471
It's so amazing to see, you know,

00:02:01.471 --> 00:02:04.117
Emiratis and non-Emiratis
both get out in the water,

00:02:04.117 --> 00:02:05.455
and have an absolutely great time,

00:02:05.455 --> 00:02:08.065
sharing the same experience.

00:02:08.065 --> 00:02:08.898
- [Scott] At the end of the day,

00:02:08.898 --> 00:02:11.469
we're trying to share
this love for the sport,

00:02:11.469 --> 00:02:12.602
and we do teach Emiratis,

00:02:12.602 --> 00:02:15.202
as well as eastern and
western expatriates,

00:02:15.202 --> 00:02:16.172
and once you're in there,

00:02:16.172 --> 00:02:18.172
you never wanna get out.

